      {
        "id": 46771,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-27T21:36:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"UXM266\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/uxm266/48/1966_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> UXM266:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Vyolynce wrote:</b><br><blockquote>If she puts out a lot of heat I bet there are interesting interactions between her and AZ...\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nNo one wants to comment on this? I guess I will!&nbsp;Ummm... His suit needs to be made of tephlon to avoid chaffing? no no.... Hmmm I'll get back on this/...\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>So we're agreed, then, that Absolute Zero has an addiction to Friction?</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I think the Abs/Proletariat rivalry stems from their motivations.&nbsp; Zero doesn't want to be a hero.&nbsp; He's doing superhero community service so he can pay off his suit and live a \"normal\" life.&nbsp; Proletariat is a man of the people and for the people.&nbsp; I think Absolute Zero embodies everything he hates about America.&nbsp; Zero, in his eyes, is a slave to the capitalist machine and only wants to do anything so that he can get ahead in his own life and do what he wants to do with little to no regard to the people around him.&nbsp; Granted, I think we all know that there is more to Abs than that, but I could see that conclusion being reached.&nbsp; I really like the impersonal nature of their rivalry.&nbsp; It reminds me of The Flash and Captian Cold (before Captain Cold's AWFUL reinterpretation in the New 52).</p>",
