      {
        "id": 46773,
        "name": "EvanDan55",
        "username": "EvanDan55",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/evandan55/{size}/2374_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-27T21:41:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Reckless\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/48/2467_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Reckless:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;I think the Abs/Proletariat rivalry stems from their motivations.&nbsp; Zero doesn't want to be a hero.&nbsp; He's doing superhero community service so he can pay off his suit and live a \"normal\" life.&nbsp; Proletariat is a man of the people and for the people.&nbsp; I think Absolute Zero embodies everything he hates about America.&nbsp; Zero, in his eyes, is a slave to the capitalist machine and only wants to do anything so that he can get ahead in his own life and do what he wants to do with little to no regard to the people around him.&nbsp; Granted, I think we all know that there is more to Abs than that, but I could see that conclusion being reached.&nbsp; I really like the impersonal nature of their rivalry.&nbsp; It reminds me of The Flash and Captian Cold (before Captain Cold's AWFUL reinterpretation in the New 52).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's a good point. It'd be interesting to see what their first encounter would have been like. I'm assuming that all the heroes paired off with their counterparts, so I wonder what it would have been like when these two men who have no reason to hate each other personally came into conflict. I'm sure it was one-sided at first. AZ probably just wanted to be done with the fighting, whereas Proletariat wanted to bring down AZ because of what he represents. AZ probably started to hate Proletariat just because he didn't like him.</p>",
